RRCAT provides a robust infrastructure for scientific computing, encompassing high-end servers, clusters, and advanced software tools. This infrastructure is accessible 24/7 via RRCATNet and utilizes Virtual Network Computing (VNC) for remote graphical access.  
Four computing clusters with a combined sustained performance of 240.18 Teraflops (TF) are available for parallel computing. TORQUE serves as the cluster resource manager, while Maui schedules jobs, ensuring efficient resource utilization.  
Kshitij-5 is the latest addition to RRCAT's computing facilities, offering significant computational power advanced features.  
